<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.623 mln bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.623 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton output from the 1996/97 (July-June) crop reached a provisional 8.623 million 375-lb bales by March 20, down from 9.844 million bales in the same year-ago period, the state-run Cotton Export Corporation said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Devlivery and ginning figures in million bales (with year-ago figures given in brackets):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.556 (8.107)  2.067 (1.737)  8.623 (9.844)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.514 (8.079)  2.008 (1.683)  8.522 (9.763)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.397 (6.424)  1.739 (1.189)  7.137 (7.613)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.005 (0.999)  0.0004(0.402)  0.005 (1.401)</p>
<p> Unsold	   1.153 (0.684)  0.327 (0.145)  1.480 (0.829)</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
